dragonmounts2:guide_book.text.home=Welcome to the §4Dragon Mounts 2 Add-On§r! For help, check out~LINEBREAK~§l§oGet Started§r!~LINEBREAK~~LINEBREAK~§1(You can craft this book again using 1 Dragon Scale of any kind with a Book)§r~LINEBREAK~~LINEBREAK~Join the §dDragon Mounts§r community!~LINEBREAK~Discord: §8discord.com/invite/Ewm8aTTJ3K§r~LINEBREAK~Bluesky: §8@dragonmounts.bsky.social§r~LINEBREAK~TikTok: §8tiktok.com/@dragonmountsmod§r~LINEBREAK~Instagram: §8instagram.com/dragonmountsmod§r~LINEBREAK~X: §8x.com/dragonmountsmod§r
dragonmounts2:guide_book.text.page_1_1=There are many §5dragons§r to choose from, and each one has its own unique §dbreath§r.~LINEBREAK~~LINEBREAK~Choose your dragon wisely and prepare for an adventure unlike any other.
dragonmounts2:guide_book.text.page_1_2=To tame a dragon, you must first find a dragon egg and hatch it.~LINEBREAK~~LINEBREAK~Once hatched, feed your dragon until your able to make it sit  you, and then you can begin riding it. The bond will not come instantly, though, and your dragon may test you before it accepts you fully.
dragonmounts2:guide_book.text.page_1_3=When your dragon is ready, you can craft and equip a saddle,chest or dragon armour.~LINEBREAK~~LINEBREAK~Use the saddle and interact with your dragon to begin riding, You can also interact with your dragon to equip dragon armour and a chest for extra storage.
dragonmounts2:guide_book.text.page_1_4=
dragonmounts2:guide_book.text.page_1_5=Dragons come in many different appearances, and most have three or four variants, with many having three.~LINEBREAK~~LINEBREAK~Here is a useful tip: you can change your dragon's appearance by using §l:_input_key.use:§r on it with a §9Variation Orb§r.
dragonmounts2:guide_book.text.page_2_1=Use §l:_input_key.use:§r to:~LINEBREAK~~LINEBREAK~- Feed your dragon a variety of foods~LINEBREAK~- Equip a saddle, dragon armour, and chest~LINEBREAK~- Start riding your dragon
dragonmounts2:guide_book.text.page_2_2=Movement should remain smooth and steady.~LINEBREAK~~LINEBREAK~Turn gently, keep your balance, and let your dragon carry you with confidence.
dragonmounts2:guide_book.text.page_2_3=Interaction matters most when you are close to your mount.~LINEBREAK~~LINEBREAK~Use your tools carefully, speak calmly, and never rush the bond.
dragonmounts2:guide_book.text.page_2_4=Your dragon has two abilities at the moment. One is the dragon breath attack. To breathe fire, you must be riding your dragon and holding down §l:_input_key.jump:§r to use it in the direction you are looking.~LINEBREAK~~LINEBREAK~The other is the bite attack, which only happens when you hit a target. Depending on how strong the target is, your dragon may breathe fire at it.~LINEBREAK~~LINEBREAK~Toggle the environmental effects in the settings if you would like the environment not to be damaged.
dragonmounts2:guide_book.text.page_2_5=Practice often and learn the rhythm of your dragon.~LINEBREAK~~LINEBREAK~The more you use the controls with patience, the easier every flight becomes.
dragonmounts2:guide_book.text.page_3_1=Training a dragon takes time and consistency.~LINEBREAK~~LINEBREAK~Feed it regularly, keep it safe, and interact with it often so it learns to recognise you as its keeper.
dragonmounts2:guide_book.text.page_3_2=Trust grows when the dragon feels secure.~LINEBREAK~~LINEBREAK~Let it come to you first, reward calm behaviour, and avoid sudden actions that may scare it.
dragonmounts2:guide_book.text.page_3_3=Use food as a reward for good behaviour.~LINEBREAK~~LINEBREAK~Give the right food at the right time, and your dragon will begin to associate you with safety and positive results.
dragonmounts2:guide_book.text.page_3_4=Handle your dragon calmly and with purpose.~LINEBREAK~~LINEBREAK~Move slowly, use the correct tools, and do not force it into actions it does not understand.
dragonmounts2:guide_book.text.page_3_5=Progress is measured by repetition and patience.~LINEBREAK~~LINEBREAK~If your dragon responds well, keep the routine steady and build from small successes.
dragonmounts2:guide_book.text.page_4_1=Baby dragons need more frequent care than adults.~LINEBREAK~~LINEBREAK~Keep them fed, protected from danger, and in a safe place where they can rest and grow.
dragonmounts2:guide_book.text.page_4_2=Young dragons should be kept warm, sheltered, and in a calm routine.~LINEBREAK~~LINEBREAK~A stable environment helps them settle and reduces stress.
dragonmounts2:guide_book.text.page_4_3=Feed hatchlings on a regular schedule and watch for signs of hunger, weakness, or unusual behaviour.~LINEBREAK~~LINEBREAK~Consistent care is more important than large amounts of food.
dragonmounts2:guide_book.text.page_4_4=Keep baby dragons away from hostile mobs and from rough handling.~LINEBREAK~~LINEBREAK~A quiet area with enough space helps them stay healthy while they grow.
dragonmounts2:guide_book.text.page_4_5=As they age, baby dragons become stronger and easier to manage.~LINEBREAK~~LINEBREAK~Good care early on makes later training much easier.
dragonmounts2:guide_book.text.page_5_1=The Dragon Forge is used to craft gear for both you and your dragon.~LINEBREAK~~LINEBREAK~It is the main place for making armour, tools, flutes, and other useful items.
dragonmounts2:guide_book.text.page_5_2=Use armour to improve protection for your dragon or for yourself.~LINEBREAK~~LINEBREAK~Equip gear that matches the situation, especially before combat or long travel.
dragonmounts2:guide_book.text.page_5_3=Crafting unlocks better equipment and more options as you progress.~LINEBREAK~~LINEBREAK~Gather materials, compare recipes, and make the items that best suit your current needs.
dragonmounts2:guide_book.text.page_5_4=Saddles and other riding gear make travel easier and more controlled.~LINEBREAK~~LINEBREAK~Make sure your dragon is properly equipped before setting off on a journey.
dragonmounts2:guide_book.text.page_5_5=The more useful items you craft, the more flexible your playstyle becomes.~LINEBREAK~~LINEBREAK~Build gear that supports your preferred way of exploring, fighting, and travelling.
dragonmounts2:guide_book.text.page_6_1=Use the settings menu to adjust how the add-on feels while you play.~LINEBREAK~~LINEBREAK~Change options to improve comfort, clarity, and performance.
dragonmounts2:guide_book.text.page_6_2=§l§nDragon Mounts Team§r~LINEBREAK~- Tomanex - Owner, Lead Developer, Designer~LINEBREAK~- Grummboy2 - Lead Coder, Designer~LINEBREAK~- Myro - Assistant Coder~LINEBREAK~- Moaswies - Assistant Coder~LINEBREAK~- EquinoxTheWingedWolf - Lead Designer~LINEBREAK~~LINEBREAK~§l§nContributors§r~LINEBREAK~- JDSK0ala - Originally forming the team~LINEBREAK~- Bluestenonycho64 - Concept Artist~LINEBREAK~- EnderHeart - Shadow design~LINEBREAK~- Mr. Goofy - Retired Coder~LINEBREAK~- NightScale5755 - Retired contributor~LINEBREAK~- MiahDragon - Retired contributor~LINEBREAK~~LINEBREAK~§l§nSupporting Artists/Designers§r~LINEBREAK~- Kingdomall - Retired Artist and Lead Designer, Old Dragon designs, Old Shield designs~LINEBREAK~- Shannieann - Retired Designer, Old Nether Dragon designs, Old Terra Dragon designs, Old Zombie Dragon designs, Old Sword designs, Old Essence Gem designs~LINEBREAK~- UkanGundan - Retired Designer and SFX Artist, Water Dragon sounds, Old Sunlight Dragon designs, Old Moonlight Dragon designs~LINEBREAK~- FlaemWing - Retired Designer, Old Nest Block design, Old Tool Equipment designs, Old Dragon Armor Item designs~LINEBREAK~- cesar_zorak - Retired Designer, Old Ice Dragon design, Old Dragon Armor Model design, Old Breed Types designs~LINEBREAK~- Majty/GuineaOwl - Retired Designer, Old Amulet designs~LINEBREAK~- Crafty411 - Retired Designer, Old Ice Dragon design
dragonmounts2:guide_book.text.page_6_3=Visual settings affect how readable and immersive the world feels.~LINEBREAK~~LINEBREAK~Adjust them so you can spot dragons, terrain, and effects more clearly.
dragonmounts2:guide_book.text.page_6_4=Preferences are there to make the add-on feel more natural to you.~LINEBREAK~~LINEBREAK~Spend a moment adjusting them so the gameplay feels comfortable and consistent.

~LINEBREAK~- Here are things your dragon will enjoy eating; these items can be used for both healing and breeding:~LINEBREAK~~LINEBREAK~ - Raw Chicken~LINEBREAK~ - Raw Beef~LINEBREAK~ - Raw Porkchop~LINEBREAK~ - Raw Mutton~LINEBREAK~ - Raw Rabbit~LINEBREAK~ - Raw Salmon~LINEBREAK~ - Raw Cod~LINEBREAK~ - Pufferfish~LINEBREAK~ - Bucket of Axolotl~LINEBREAK~ - Bucket of Cod~LINEBREAK~ - Bucket of Salmon~LINEBREAK~ - Bucket of Tadpole~LINEBREAK~ - Bucket of Pufferfish~LINEBREAK~ - Brown Egg~LINEBREAK~ - Blue Egg~LINEBREAK~ - Egg~LINEBREAK~ - Cooked Chicken~LINEBREAK~ - Cooked Beef~LINEBREAK~ - Cooked Porkchop~LINEBREAK~ - Cooked Mutton~LINEBREAK~ - Cooked Rabbit~LINEBREAK~ - Cooked Salmon~LINEBREAK~ - Cooked Cod~LINEBREAK~ - Cooked Mutton~LINEBREAK~

